## Changes

- 2026-10-29 The preview iframe rendered every page unstyled. Adding the inline splash `<style>` to `index.html` gave Tauri a reason to hash `style-src`, and CSP ignores `'unsafe-inline'` as soon as a hash is present; `srcdoc` inherits the host document's CSP, so all preview pages lost their inline styles while the app shell (linked CSS, `'self'`) was unaffected. `dangerousDisableAssetCspModification` now covers `style-src` alongside `script-src`.
- 2026-10-29 The launch splash now follows real loading: the 2500 ms floor is gone and it leaves the moment `pebble:gateway-ready` arrives. The progress bar creeps toward 92% over 1600 ms and jumps to 100% on readiness, so a slow gateway still shows a moving bar rather than a stalled one. The 12 s cap stays.
- 2026-10-29 Added a launch splash. Three inclined elliptical tracks carry travelling light arcs (dash offset walking the path, geometry never rotates), a 5px core breathes at the centre inside two tick rings, and the exit collapses every orbit into the core while one ring expands and fades. It is inlined in `index.html` so it paints before the module graph loads, keeps its own dark palette rather than following `data-theme`, and leaves on `pebble:gateway-ready` with a 2500 ms floor and a 12 s cap.
- 2026-10-29 The prototype renderers in `render.ts` were removed: `renderTool`, `renderAvatar`, `renderWho`, `renderThinking`, `badgeFor`, `toolClass` and `termBlock` had no callers since tool calls became a Vue component, and `AVATAR_SVG` went with them. `ToolState`, `ToolCallView` and `AttachmentView` stay because `wire.ts` imports them.
- 2026-10-29 Every launch showed a screen of prototype content for as long as the sidecar took to boot, then wiped it in one frame. `plan` and `permissions` opened with sample steps and three pending requests, `runtime.js` fired a fake "Connected to gateway" toast at 900 ms and a "Plan created" demo at 1500 ms that also opened the plan slip, and a `?seed=1` switch could seed the transcript. All of it is removed: the plan and permission stores start closed and empty, `StreamItem`/`StreamKind` moved into `stream.ts`, `messageMock.ts` and its `mockStream` array are deleted, and `resetDemoState`/`__PEBBLE_DEMO`/`demoOn` no longer exist.
- 2026-10-29 The tool-call status word no longer sits permanently on a successful call: it fades in with the duration on hover, since the rail has already gone quiet and the tick marks the seam. Running, failed and cancelled calls keep it on screen, because a failure must never depend on a hover to be noticed.
- 2026-10-29 Tool calls render as trace rows: the card border, badge and icon chip are gone, replaced by a 1px rail whose node is the tool glyph. A running call walks a spark down the rail and pings the node ring; a settled one fades the rail and drops a tick at the seam. Name, argument, duration and a lowercase status word sit on one line, with duration fading in on hover. Expansion still animates through `grid-template-rows` with the output hanging off a hairline under the node. The index-row experiment and its `toolSeq` numbering were removed.
- 2026-10-29 Tool calls render as index rows instead of cards. `StreamToolCard.vue` puts a two-digit sequence, a 13px glyph, the name, the argument, a lowercase status word and the duration on one line; the chevron only appears on hover or when open, and expansion animates through `grid-template-rows` with the output hanging off a hairline indented to the name column. `StreamMessage.vue` numbers calls among tool blocks only. No border, no badge, no icon chip — status is a word and a colour, so a long run of calls reads as a list rather than a stack.
- 2026-10-29 Paragraph runs between thinking and tool cards kept a blinking caret after the turn ended. `finishLive` rewrote only the tail block into markdown and never cleared the `caret: true` those blocks are created with, so only a session switch removed the cursor. Every `raw` block now settles when the turn does.
- 2026-10-29 Every turn ran in the sidecar's install directory: `sendPrompt` posted `prompt.submit` without `project_path`, and `chat_stream` answered `self._current_project_path = project_path or os.getcwd()`. In a packaged build cwd is where the sidecar exe lives, so the system prompt announced `frontend/src-tauri/target/release` regardless of the project, and each turn overwrote the value `project.set_active` had just installed. Repaired at all four points: `sendPrompt` sends `project_path`, `chat_stream` keeps the existing value instead of falling back to cwd and routes a changed path through `set_project_path` (which also syncs the tool executor, truncation dir, whitelist and MCP config), `_ensure_service()` restores `projects.json` `active` on first use, and `handle_prompt_submit` resolves a missing value through request → active → service path.
- 2026-10-29 Quick notes had no click behaviour. Each row now appends its text to the composer through `appendToComposer`, which writes `#composerTa` directly and dispatches `input` so autosize and the token meter follow (the field has no v-model), adds a space only when the existing text does not already end in whitespace, and leaves the caret at the end. Rows are keyboard reachable and the delete button stops propagation so removing a note does not also insert it.
- 2026-10-29 Compaction left the context ring at its pre-fold height until the next prompt: the ring reads the last call's `latest_input_tokens`, which still described the old transcript, while `session.compress` already returned the measured `after.tokens` and the frontend only consumed the `messages` counters. `compressSession` now writes `after.tokens` into `usage.contextTokens`, clears `usage.contextOut`, and recomputes `contextPct`, so the window drops as soon as the fold lands.
- 2026-10-29 The usage ring drew a fixed two-thirds arc no matter how full the window was: `stroke-dashoffset: 33` was hardcoded in CSS while the label beside it printed the real `contextPct`, and `animation: ring-draw … both` froze that value at first paint so later updates could never reach the arc. The offset now comes from `contextPct` as an inline style over `pathLength="100"`, the fixed value and its keyframes are gone, and a transition lets the arc settle on the reported share.
- 2026-10-29 A session created seconds ago surfaced at the bottom of the switcher under "Earlier". `_row_to_list_item` exposes the start time as `started_at` and sends `last_message_at: null` for a session with no turns, while `toSession` only looked for `updated_at`/`created_at` and let the chain collapse to 0 — and 0 buckets to "Earlier". Zero now counts as absent and `started_at` is read, so a fresh session buckets under Today.
- 2026-10-29 Switching projects left the previous project's conversations on screen: `session.list` was requested without `project_path` in both `fetchSessions` and `bootstrap`, so the list was always the union of every project. Both are scoped to `projects.active` now, `bootstrap` resolves the registry before asking, and a project with no stored session goes through `createSession()` so the new row keeps its `project_path` and appears in the switcher at once.
- 2026-10-29 The project switcher shipped as prototype markup: `pebbleagent`, `E:\pebbleagent`, `main` and the three list rows were literal strings, and `Switch`, `+`, `×` and `adopt` had no listeners, so a typed path went nowhere. It is now data-driven — `projects` in the store, `refreshProjects` / `addProject` / `switchProject` / `removeProject` in `wire.ts` — and `switchProject` re-runs `bootstrap()` because every session row belongs to the project that was active when it was created.
- 2026-10-29 The island's tok/s read `— tok/s` for entire replies: `paintAgent` never wrote `plain` while streaming, and the rate is computed from that field. It is now written on every paint, which also fixes the context split and Copy mid-stream. The live row is found by scanning back for `streaming` instead of assuming the last item, so a row appended after it cannot blank the headline.
- 2026-10-29 The expanded reasoning block carried the global 8px scrollbar, which reads as a slab beside 11px text. It now has its own 4px bar: nearly invisible at rest, `--faint` once the paragraph is hovered, `--accent` while the thumb is dragged.
- 2026-10-29 Reasoning rails now stop animating per run instead of per turn: `paintAgent` marks only the tail thinking block `live`, so a completed run turns static as soon as the next block lands. A turn that reasons five times used to keep five infinite scan animations alive until the whole reply finished.
- 2026-10-29 The live-run headline now distinguishes `Writing…` from `Thinking…` when no tool is in flight, by looking at the kind of the last block on the streaming row instead of printing one word for both. The expanded `tool` row follows the same split (`writing` / `thinking`).
- 2026-10-29 The live-run island reported `Thinking…` and an `idle` tool row through every turn that had no todo list, because both were derived from `plan.steps`, which only `todos.update` fills. `liveTool` now reads the last tool card off the streaming row's blocks, so the headline names the call in flight and the expanded row shows its argument and status; the plan remains the fallback and `step X of Y` only renders when a plan exists.
- 2026-10-29 Deleting a message was only real for rows that already had a stored id. `finishLive` kept the local `live-3` id, so the numeric guard in `deleteMessage` never fired and an AI reply came back on the next reload; it now adopts `message.complete.message_id`. `deleteMessage` also reports local-only removals instead of staying silent, clears `pendingUser` so `user_message.saved` cannot re-add a prompt the reader just deleted, and decrements the header count once the gateway confirms.
- 2026-10-29 The transcript refused to scroll up once following was added. The `scroll` listener went through the same handler as the height observer, so `follow()` ran before the measurement that would have cleared `stick` and dragged the reader back on every wheel tick. Scroll events now only re-measure; growth is the single path that may move the offset, and `follow()` additionally stops when the offset fell below the last known one.
- 2026-10-29 Transcript order was wrong in three places at once. Live reasoning held one shared block and `unshift`-ed it to the head, so every later run folded into the first card and the whole answer piled underneath; tool cards were spliced above the open text run instead of appended where the call happened; and `finishLive` re-ordered the settled array into reasoning + text + tools. All three now append in arrival order and merge only into a trailing block of the same kind, and `finishLive` settles just the open tail. A stopped turn also settles itself now: still-running tool cards flip to `cancelled` both live and when restored from the transcript, and the row closes with a dashed `interrupted` marker.
- 2026-10-29 Orbit got its own desktop shell. `frontend/src-tauri/` is a copy of the Rust layer (sidecar launcher, `get_gateway_token`, capabilities, icons) under a distinct package name `pebble-orbit-shell` and identifier `com.pebble.agent.orbit`, so it builds into `frontend/dist` and installs beside the ui-gui-vue3 app instead of overwriting it. The window is undecorated: `OrbitalBar` gained `data-tauri-drag-region` on the strip and its inert children, and the three window buttons now call `plugin:window|minimize`, `toggle_maximize` and `close` instead of raising a prototype toast.
- 2026-10-29 The LLM pane regained the OpenCode Go request-shaping block. `MODES` had been `['thinking', 'opencode-go', 'session hdr']`, which treated a section title and an input label as mutually exclusive reasoning modes, and the rest of the block was missing outright. It now reads `['thinking', 'effort_only']`, with `session hdr`, `max effort`, `reasoning mode` and `extra headers` below a labelled rule; `maxEffort` also gets a state slot, a read-back from `model.options` and a field in `model.provider.save`.
- 2026-10-29 Tool cards had two problems with one cause. Restored cards opened onto nothing because `add_tool_message` inserted an empty `content` column: only the live `tool.complete` event carried `result_text`, so the transcript recorded that a tool ran but never what it returned. The insert now stores the output, `server.py` passes it through, and rows written before this change say `output not recorded` instead of opening empty. Read tools also stopped printing their payload: `read_file` and friends show `already read` once they succeed, because the file still reaches the model through `result_text` and the stored row, and only the card withholds it.
- 2026-10-29 Three fixes after the restart. The pricing table came up empty because `UsagePane` mounts before the socket handshake and `getConfig` refuses to run while disconnected; the loader now retries for a few seconds instead of leaving the pane blank for the whole session. The snapshot timeline rendered every raw record, so a session with 33 edits showed 33 identical rows - neighbouring entries from the same tool within a minute now merge into one with a `xN` chip, the tail hides behind a `show N earlier` control, and the header reads `10 of 33 snapshots`. Reverting a merged entry reverts every path it collected. Palette and accent were verified to persist: switching to dark and picking a swatch survive a hard reload.
- 2026-10-29 Four panels were reading the prototype instead of the gateway. The header counted rendered bubbles (27) rather than the rows the session holds (3895+), because it filtered `streamState.items`; it now reports `sessionState.messageCount`, seeded from the resume payload and incremented as a turn settles. Appearance persisted nothing usable: the palette was written to `localStorage` but never read back and the accent swatch had no handler at all, so both are now restored before the first frame (silently, without the ripple) and the swatch writes `pebble-orbit-accent`. The Files pane's snapshot timeline was three invented rows with no backend behind them; `session.snapshots` now groups the snapshot records by `snapshot_id` (one entry per tool call, with file count, path list and revert state) and the pane renders those, falling back to `no snapshots yet`. The pricing table was four hardcoded cards with a fake `DATA` map in `runtime.js`; the pane now loads `config.get('pricing')` (reading the table under either the root or `pricing`), renders one card per model with the base / peak / off period selector, and saves through `pricing.save` with the raw per-period blocks so `pricing_peak` and `pricing_tier_high` survive the round trip.
- 2026-10-29 ```` ```mermaid ```` fences used to land in the code renderer, so a diagram arrived as a wall of highlighted keywords. `splitBlocks` now gives them their own `kind: 'mermaid'` block (the open fence stays streaming), `MermaidCard.vue` renders it, and the renderer is imported lazily so the 3.5MB mermaid bundle never enters the first paint. The card picks its colours from the live CSS variables on every render, which is what makes it follow the accent and the dark theme; before rendering it normalises the Chinese quotation marks and double angle brackets models like to emit, and a parse failure shows the first error line instead of tearing the row apart. Its dependency closure (105 packages, mermaid 11.17.2) was copied from `ui-gui-vue3/node_modules`, so no network install was involved.
- 2026-10-29 The preview could show a page but not take a note on it. The comment layer is now part of the injected document: `previewBridge.ts` ships the picker (hover ring, element picker, editor, numbered markers), `buildSrcdoc` inlines its CSS and script next to the CSP and the capture bridge, and the frame's `pebble-stage-ready` message switches it on with the app's palette read from the live theme. Annotations come back as `pebble-feedback-update` and land on `previewState.comments`; switching files or reloading drops them, because a selector belongs to one document. Getting them to the model reuses the shell's channel: `respondClarify` runs the answers through `mergePreviewComments`, which replaces the option that asks for a change with a `Modify\n\n[HTML Page Feedback] ...` block listing every annotation's selector, tag, original text and comment, and clears the list once the gateway accepts the reply. A change event on the file already on screen now re-reads it after a 400ms settle instead of reloading per event.
- 2026-10-29 The preview stage was a design mockup: three invented file names, an iframe whose `srcdoc` was a hand-written usage card, a hardcoded output path, and a Save PNG button that painted the same fake card onto a canvas. It now runs on data. `preview.ts` scans `@pebble-file:` directives out of `streamState.items[].plain` (gated on an html/svg extension so prose about the directive registers nothing), registers one entry per file, and reads the active one through `file.read_text`, trying the relative path and then the project-root-anchored one. The source is injected with the shell's CSP as the first head node and with the bundled `html-to-image` plus a postMessage bridge before `</body>`, so Save PNG asks the sandboxed frame to rasterise itself instead of drawing a substitute. Device presets, viewport label, size label, path label, Code view and the empty state are all bound to that state, and `file.change` marks a background file stale or reloads the one on screen.
- 2026-10-29 Message rows showed five-digit numbers where the clock belongs (`28504 · sent`, `deepseek-v4.1-flash · 89365`). `messages.created_at` is an epoch float (`REAL NOT NULL` in the gateway store) but `buildHistory` sliced it as if it were `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`, so `slice(11, 16)` returned the fractional digits. `dateOf`/`clockOf` in `render.ts` now normalise seconds and milliseconds into a `Date` once, `buildHistory` reads the wall clock from them, and `StreamTimeline.stampOf` goes through the same helper instead of keeping its own copy of the split.
