## An interrupted turn keeps what it already said

- Transport failures (`peer closed connection without sending complete message
  body (incomplete chunked read)` and friends) never reach `chat_completed`, so
  the partial text lived only in memory: the transcript kept it until the next
  reload, then showed nothing but the error line
- Agent side: `except Exception` now persists the accumulated reply to
  `agent_chat.db` (in-flight chunk flushed into `execution_order` first, fresh
  uuid) and ships the same text on the `error` event
- Gateway: `_persist_interrupted_reply` writes body + `**Error:** ...` as one
  assistant row with `interrupted=1` and the agent-side uuid, from both the
  `error` event branch and the outer `except`; the generator-ended fallback save
  is gated on `elif not assistant_saved`, so the reply is not stored twice and
  no `message.complete` follows to wipe the marker; the event carries `content`
  / `reasoning` / `execution_order` / `message_id` / `interrupted`
- Orbit shell (`frontend/`, the only front end; `ui-gui-vue3` was deleted):
  the error branch appends only the tail the live row is missing, flips
  in-flight tool cards to cancelled, and settles with `interrupted` +
  `message_id`, so the row the user sees is the row the database will rebuild on reload
- Cancel now reads the in-flight `consumer.content` too, so a cancel can no
  longer append the previous round's text twice
- Tests: `tests/test_chat_stream_e2e.py` (transport-error case) and
  `tests/test_interrupted_reply.py` (row format / uuid / fallback)
- 2026-10-28

