## The backend runs on macOS in web mode

- `run_backend.py` calls `SetPriorityClass` only when `sys.platform == "win32"`:
  `ctypes.windll` does not exist on POSIX, so the unguarded call aborted startup
  before the gateway was even imported
- `start_backend.sh` is the POSIX counterpart of `start_backend.bat`: dependency
  probe, `lsof` port cleanup, backend launch, socket-based readiness wait, trap
  cleanup and single-key stop. LF endings, ASCII only. The batch file is untouched
- `powershell` is platform-gated: `_PLATFORM_ONLY` in `tool_definitions.py` drops it
  from the schema off Windows (46 tools on win32, 45 elsewhere), and
  `_tool_powershell` returns an error there for history replays and direct RPC calls
- `tests/test_code_agent_prompt_contract.py` builds its tool universe as the schema
  set plus `_PLATFORM_ONLY`, so the prompt contract still holds on a platform where
  the tool is hidden rather than absent
